From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] nexus_engine: install the engine crash handler when the
 log starts

NEXUS loads the engine in-process and the Go runtime sets SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX, so a native
crash inside the engine ended NEXUS with no dialog, no Windows Error Reporting dump and no
log line. Lichii's own front-ends install Common::Windows::InstallCrashHandler; do the same
when the engine first starts its log (session or shader preparation): a "Host crash" Critical
line with module+offset stack and thread name, a flushed log, and eden_crash.dmp in the log
directory (or EDEN_NX2_CRASH_DUMP). Nothing changes until a crash happens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
